\noindent TES system choices are often driven by multiple factors, dependencies, and limitations: required temperature levels, storage duration, available space and integration, economic and operational aspects, climate, and thermal demand characteristics (Tafere, 2026). In this study, the thermal demand profile (load curve) of a building will serve as a primary criterion for determining the appropriate TES system.

