\subsubsection*{Separate Heating and Cooling Aggregation} Once the thermal demand is calculated for each zone per time-step, you can determine the peak power requirements for the TES system. By summing the heating demands across all zones at each time-step, the maximum aggregate value over the year identifies the peak heating power requirement. For cooling, the same logic applies, where the most negative value of $Q_{\text{total}}(t)$ represents the peak cooling load.
\\

\begin{equation}
    Q_{\text{total}}(t) = \sum_{i=1}^{n} Q_{\text{zone},i}(t)
\end{equation}

