\subsubsection*{Data format} The required thermal demand dataset is structured as a DataFrame (\textit{see table 2}), indexing the zone's thermal demand at discrete intervals (time-steps). A high-fidelity demand profile is foundational to the framework, as the precision of the input data directly dictates the accuracy of the resulting TES dimensions. This means that the more accurate the demand per zone can be calculated (as close to reality as possible), the more efficiently the thermal system including buffer can be sized.
\\

\noindent While an annual dataset captures seasonal fluctuations in thermal loads, the length of each time-step is just as important (high-time resolution). The smaller the time-step, the more effectively the model captures peak demand spikes and operational behaviours, without these fluctuations being masked by a big time-step. 
