\subsubsection{Load Duration Curve} A Load Duration Curve (LDC) gives insight into a buildings yearly thermal demand. A load model represents a system's energy demand over a given period and is used to assess capacity adequacy. Load models are generally classified as load duration curve (LDC) models or chronological (time-series) models. An LDC is formed by sorting hourly peak loads in descending order. An annual LDC (8760 hours) provides the most accurate representation (Almutairi et al., 2015). 
\\

