\subsubsection{Passive Strategy: Thermal Mass} Integrating the thermal mass of a building into its operational strategy provides a more sophisticated thermal management system than relying on active climate control alone. Regarding temperature set-points in combination with thermal mass, the following variables can be distinguished: 
\\

\begin{itemize}
    \item \makebox[1.7cm][l]{\textcolor{myblue}{$T_{set}$}:} The temperature set-point of zone $n$
    \item \makebox[1.7cm][l]{\textcolor{myblue}{$T_{swing}$}:} The allowed temperature differential compared to $T_{set}$ for zone $n$ (optional)
    \item \makebox[1.7cm][l]{\textcolor{myblue}{$T_{min}$}:} The minimum allowed temperature of zone $n$ (also possible: $T_{min}$ = $T_{set}$)
    \item \makebox[1.7cm][l]{\textcolor{myblue}{$T_{max}$}:} The maximum allowed temperature of zone $n$ (also possible: $T_{max}$ = $T_{set}$)
\end{itemize}
