\subsubsection*{Optimizer} To determine the optimal thermal energy storage (TES) capacity, the optimizer employs a binary search algorithm that iteratively divides the search space to converge on the most efficient solution. The simulation engine provides hourly temperature and state-of-charge data, which the optimizer uses to test specific capacity values against defined temperature constraints. 
\\

\noindent By systematically checking for temperature limit violations, the algorithm identifies the smallest successful capacity, designated as $E_{max\_gap}$, which is then converted into the final volume of the TES system. This volume is directly determined by the energy density of the storage medium, which defines how much energy can be contained per unit of physical space.

