\subsubsection {System Choice} For event-driven peaks, a stratified buffer tank is selected due to its high power density and low thermal lag. While other TES media may offer higher energy density, the water-based buffer tank excels in its ability to meet rapid discharge requirements without the heat-transfer bottlenecks associated with solid-state or phase-change systems. Moreover, design principles leading to this choice of TES include: energy-efficient and environmentally friendly, low-maintenance, low operating costs, and compatible with fully electric heat pumps. The stratified buffer tanks are the centralized TES units supplied by heat pumps, and providing the emitter of the zones with thermal energy.
