\subsubsection{Stratified Buffer Tank} Effective TES operation utilizes the inherent density differences of water to maintain thermal layers. This results in a vertical temperature profile where hot water remains at the top and cold water at the bottom, separated by a mid-level thermocline. Research indicates that maximizing the temperature difference and optimizing the tank's aspect ratio are primary drivers for maintaining high stratification quality (Bahnfleth \& Musser, 1998). Stratification is reduced through fluid mixing caused by convection and through thermocline movement resulting from load imbalances (Haller et al., 2009). 
\\

