\noindent 2. The following formula for $PV\_kVA_{i}$ converts the direct light onto the PV panels into the electrical capacity produced by the (300 $m^2$) PV system (NEN-EN-IEC, 2021):
\\

\begin{equation}
\textit{PV\_kVA}(t) = \frac{I_{\text{poa}}(t) \cdot A \cdot \eta \cdot PR \cdot (1 - D)}{1000}
\end{equation}
\\

Where: 
\begin{itemize}
    \item $A$: Total surface area of 300 m²
    \item $\eta$: Efficiency (0.20), based on the 200 Wp/m² ($200/1000$, according to STC by (IEC, 2020))
    \item $PR$: Performance Ratio (0.78), accounting for the "moderate ventilation" and inverter losses.
    \item Degradation factor (0.995), accounting for the 0.50\% annual ageing
    \item $1000$: The divisor to convert the result from Watts to kilo-Volt-Amperes (kVA).
\end{itemize}
\\

