        \midrule
        Fixed kVA split & Uses the \texttt{$HEATING\_SHARE\_INPUT$} as a rigid percentage (e.g.,, 50/50 or 70/30) regardless of the instantaneous demand in individual zones (\texttt{KVA\_SPLIT\_MODE}). \\
        Proportional split & Dynamically evaluates the actual kW demand of the zones in each specific hour and partitions the building's electrical capacity based on thermal stress (\texttt{KVA\_SPLIT\_MODE}). \\
        Mechanical floor & Enforces a 1.5 kVA (approx. 5\%) modulation minimum to maintain the thermocline and operational stability of the compressor, diverting surplus energy to the TES (\texttt{HP\_MIN\_MOD\_KVA}). \\
        Thermal drift & Simulates continuous hourly energy degradation to the environment to prevent the TES from acting as a loss-free reservoir, ensuring realistic storage behaviour (\texttt{DRIFT\_RATE}). \\
