\subsection{Optimised Volume Check} This final section automates the system sizing through an iterative bisection search method. The engine executes multiple simulation passes to find the minimum Thermal Energy Storage (TES) capacity required to maintain zone temperatures within their defined comfort boundaries, effectively eliminating thermal violations. Following this optimization, the engine performs a hydraulic stability analysis, calculating the peak net flow requirements for both heating and cooling circuits. This ensures the system remains robust during periods of high demand deficit, sizing the necessary buffer volumes to prevent infrastructure instability.
